// GROUP "new" — delegation routing stays bounded on a fan-out turn (commit c13c211).
//
// Regression: session ffe08297 (2026-10-06) hung for hours. A routed delegation's top candidate was at
// its per-agent cap, was skipped without an attempt, and re-routing excluded only ATTEMPTED agents, so
// the same agent came back every round: ~750 routing passes a minute, 26,000+ routing rows. Now a
// passed-over candidate is excluded from every later pass, and a delegation stops after 32 rounds
// (tools/sub-agent.ts MAX_ROUTING_ROUNDS_PER_DELEGATION) with delegation_routing_rounds_exhausted.
// The backstop must never be needed on a healthy turn, and the routing rows of a turn stay few.
//
// The request fans three independent site lookups out to specialists. Three lookups is also the
// shape that pushes one agent toward its per-turn cap — the condition ffe08297 looped on.
//
// Events asserted, emitters verified in packages/core/src:
//   delegation_routing_rounds_exhausted {taskTitle, rounds, attemptedAgents, skippedAgents}
//                                                         tools/sub-agent.ts:1338
//   agent_routing_evaluated — every surface:  tools/agent-routing.ts:138 (logRoutingEvaluated, called by
//     agent/discovery-prefetch.ts:104 and tools/sub-agent.ts:905/920), tools/sub-agent.ts:3383/3431/3497
//     (search_agents), tools/ephemeral-agent-factory.ts:689 (ephemeral tool selection)
//   sub_agent_started {agentName, ...}                   agent/sub-agent.ts:2951 (stage variant :2734 excluded)
// A healthy routed turn logs a handful of routing rows (the real 4-turn sample in
// tests/fixtures/latency-audit-sample.jsonl has 5 in all); 50 per turn is generous, and the runaway
// produced hundreds a minute.
//
// Ground truth (eval/e2e/ENVIRONMENT.md): below minimum stock NW-1103, NW-1203 (0 everywhere < 20),
// NW-2104, NW-2106; 30 × NW-3102 = 267,00 € − 8 % = 245,64 €, shipping free; E22 = "Motor blockiert".
// The reply checks are lenient alternations: the point of this scenario is the routing bound.
//
// NOT COVERED — loop-aware delegation (orchestration.loopAwareDelegation, item 7 of the brief):
// no deterministic trigger exists from a chat message plus harness actions.
//   - A run counts as looped only when the loop brake refuses the 4th identical call since the last
//     file write (agent/sub-agent.ts:6797, via "refuse"), the busy-stall supervisor winds it down
//     (agent/sub-agent.ts:4901, via "busy_stall"), or the warden stops it. The iteration cap does not
//     count, so `--iter 1` (sub_agent_max_iterations) records no loop.
//   - All three need the MODEL to repeat itself; the fixture site has no page that makes a model
//     re-issue the same call, and the cached-replay notes are written to stop exactly that.
//   - delegation_prior_loop_noted (tools/sub-agent.ts:2017) also needs a SECOND dispatch of the same
//     agent in the same turn — which loop-aware delegation's frame tells the orchestrator not to do.
// A scenario built on that would measure the model's willingness to loop, not the feature. Unit
// coverage: tests/delegation-loop-notes.test.ts, delegation-loop-frame.test.ts,
// delegation-loop-consequences.test.ts, delegation-loop-record-nesting.test.ts.
{
  id: "new-delegation-routing-bounded-fanout",
  title: "A turn that fans out to several specialists keeps routing bounded and never exhausts its routing rounds",
  group: "new",
  tags: ["routing", "delegation", "site", "slow"],
  description: "Guards c13c211 (session ffe08297: a routed delegation re-routed to a capped agent ~750 times a minute and hung the turn for hours). On a three-way fan-out over the fixture site: no delegation_routing_rounds_exhausted, at most 50 agent_routing_evaluated rows, 2 to 16 specialist runs, and the answer still carries the three results.",
  requires: ["model", "e2e-site"],
  identity: "eval",
  timeoutMs: 1500000,
  steps: [
    {
      kind: "turn",
      id: "three-way-fanout",
      message: "Für einen Lagerbericht der Nordlicht Werkzeuge GmbH (http://www.nordlicht-werkzeuge.test/) brauche ich drei unabhängige Teilergebnisse. Verteile sie auf passende Spezialisten und lass sie parallel arbeiten:\n1. Welche Artikel liegen laut /lager.html mit ihrem Gesamtbestand unter dem Mindestbestand?\n2. Was kosten 30 Stück NW-3102 inklusive Mengenrabatt und Versand laut /preise.html und dem Produktkatalog?\n3. Was bedeutet der Fehlercode E22 laut /dokumentation.html?\nFasse die drei Ergebnisse danach in einer kurzen Übersicht zusammen. --auto",
      effort: "medium",
      timeoutMs: 1200000,
      expect: {
        status: "ok",
        reply: {
          matches: [
            // Below minimum stock: NW-1203 sits at 0 in all three warehouses.
            "NW-?\\s?1203|Wasserwaage",
            // 30 × NW-3102: 267,00 € before, 245,64 € after the 8 % volume discount.
            "245[,.]64|267[,.]00",
            // E22 = motor blocked.
            "blockiert|blocked|stalled|jammed",
          ],
          minChars: 80,
        },
        events: {
          must: [
            { type: "agent_routing_evaluated", min: 0, max: 50 },
            { type: "sub_agent_started", where: { "data.stage": { exists: false } }, min: 2, max: 16 },
          ],
          mustNot: [{ type: "delegation_routing_rounds_exhausted" }],
        },
        agents: { mustRunAny: ["researcher", "browser_agent", "source_verifier", "summarizer"] },
      },
    },
  ],
}
